<p><%= @emails.length > 1 ? "Hi all," : "Hi there," %></p>

<p>
  <%= @whodunnit.name %> <%= "(an #{@is_manager ? "organization manager" : "Fuime admin"})" unless @whodunnit == User.system_user %> has turned on transparency mode for <%= @event.name %>.
  With transparency mode enabled:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>Unauthenticated users will be able to access a <strong>read-only</strong> version of your business.</li>
  <li>None of Fuime&apos;s pages will change for signed in team members.</li>
  <%# FUIME-DIVERGENCE: these were HCB's leak-prone fields — sponsor company
      names, ACH transfer recipients, check recipients. Fuime has no sponsors and
      originates no ACH or checks (Fuime::DisabledModules), so this listed four
      things that cannot exist here and omitted the one that actually can: a
      buyer types free text at checkout and it lands in a ledger memo. That is
      the field a venture publishing its ledger needs warning about. %>
  <li>We&apos;ll do our best to redact contact info, but we can&apos;t guarantee it doesn&apos;t show up in these
    fields:
    <ul>
      <li>Payment notes your customers type at checkout</li>
      <li>Names and descriptions of the things you sell</li>
      <li>Your storefront description</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>Your <%= link_to "announcements page", event_announcement_overview_url(@event) %> will always be visible.</li>
</ul>

<% if @can_disable_transparency %>
<p>
  Managers can disable transparency mode at any time in <%= link_to "your organization settings", edit_event_url(@event) %>.
</p>
<% end %>

<%# FUIME-DIVERGENCE: "our blog post" linked to blog.hcb.hackclub.com — an
    email from Fuime sending a Fuime user to Hack Club's blog, described as ours.
    Fuime has no blog to point at, so the sentence explains itself instead of
    borrowing somebody else's write-up (CLAUDE.md Rule 7). %>
<p>
  Managers can also turn on monthly announcements in <%= link_to "your settings", edit_event_url(@event) %>.
  If enabled, Fuime writes a new announcement each month summarising how the business did.
</p>

<p>
  From,<br>
  The Fuime Team
</p>
